<%- include("../partials/head", { title }) %>

<section class="card proper-case">
  <p class="est">legal</p>
  <h1 class="h1">Privacy Policy</h1>
  <p class="muted" style="margin-top: 0.35rem; font-size: 0.85rem">Last updated: 10-22-26</p>

  <div class="stack-section" style="margin-top: 1.5rem">

    <div class="stack-item">
      <h3>Overview</h3>
      <p>circle! e-friend finder collects only the data necessary to operate the platform. We do not sell, rent, or trade your personal information to any third party. This policy explains what we collect, how we use it, and what rights you have over your data.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="stack-item">
      <h3>Information We Collect</h3>
      <p>When you sign in via osu! OAuth, we receive your public osu! profile information (including your user ID, username, avatar, global rank, badge count, and country). We also store any profile details you voluntarily provide on this site (age, gender, bio, discord username) as well as messages you send to other users, feed posts, likes and comments you make, users you block or report, and your browse filter preferences. We only store data about people who sign in to this site. We do not collect or store data about other osu! players who have not signed in here. Our hosting provider (Google Cloud) may also process technical data such as IP addresses in server logs.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="stack-item">
      <h3>How We Use Your Information</h3>
      <p>Your data is used to display your profile to other users, power the browse and messaging features, and allow admins to moderate the platform. We do not use your data for advertising, analytics resale, or any purpose beyond operating this service.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="stack-item">
      <h3>Data Storage and Security</h3>
      <p>All user data is stored in Firebase, a Google Cloud service. Session data is stored server-side. We never store your osu! password (authentication is handled entirely through osu!'s official OAuth flow). While we take reasonable precautions, no system is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security of your data.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="stack-item">
      <h3>Visibility of Your Data</h3>
      <p>Your profile (avatar, username, rank, age, gender, bio) is visible to all logged-in users on the browse page. Your discord username is only used if you choose to enter it and is part of your profile data. Messages are private between you and the recipient. We do not make your email or osu! OAuth token visible to anyone.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="stack-item">
      <h3>Message Monitoring and Reports</h3>
      <p>Messages are not monitored in real time. Site administrators cannot search messages or browse other users' inboxes. An administrator can open a conversation only when a user has reported it from their inbox, and only to review that report. As the operator of the database, the site owner technically has access to stored data for maintenance, security, and legal compliance, but does not read messages outside of the report process or a legal requirement. Messages are stored in the database and are not end-to-end encrypted.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="stack-item">
      <h3>Deleting Your Data</h3>
      <p>You can permanently delete your account at any time from the preferences page. This removes your account, profile, bio, preferences, inbox, and the messages you sent to other users from our system. Posts or comments you made on the feed, and any reports about you, may remain until they are removed. Some residual data such as moderation records may be retained for a short period for safety purposes.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="stack-item">
      <h3>Cookies</h3>
      <p>We use a single session cookie to keep you logged in. We do not use third-party tracking cookies, advertising cookies, or any form of cross-site tracking.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="stack-item">
      <h3>Children's Privacy</h3>
      <p>This site is strictly 18+. We do not knowingly collect or retain data from anyone under the age of 18. If we become aware that a minor has created an account, we will immediately terminate it and remove associated data.</p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<%- include("../partials/foot") %>
